{"id": "EUVD-2026-97877", "enisaUuid": "b729e369-aae0-3b4e-80ce-6d85ad1a3336", "description": "Cockpit CMS 2.14.1 contains an observable timing discrepancy vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to enumerate accounts due to an incomplete timing fix in /auth/check. Attackers can post login attempts and measure response times, since existing accounts incur two bcrypt operations versus one, revealing valid usernames and email addresses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T20:55:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:52:23", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/Cockpit-HQ/Cockpit/issues/328", "https://github.com/Cockpit-HQ/Cockpit/blob/2.14.1/modules/App/Controller/Auth.php", "https://github.com/Cockpit-HQ/Cockpit/blob/2.14.1/modules/App/Helper/Auth.php", "https://github.com/Cockpit-HQ/Cockpit/commit/5d65ae7b63a261a63e8809e5fba857ef3eadb2ac", "https://github.com/Cockpit-HQ/Cockpit", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cockpit-cms-2.14.1-account-enumeration-via-timing-discrepancy-in-auth-check"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109379", "GHSA-gm9c-qwh2-h88c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2ba07b08-63b0-386e-8958-21ac29499e54", "product": {"name": "cockpit", "vendor": {"name": "cockpit-hq"}}, "product_version": "2.14.1 \u22642.14.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "44ce4acb-5d3e-35d6-b18b-d5c3860af1b7", "vendor": {"name": "cockpit-hq"}}], "isExploited": false}